    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Senior-Scientific-Officer_R000024567": {
      "title": "Senior Scientific Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $102,136 (HEW 6.1) per annum plus 17% superannuation - Appointment type:  Full-time continuing appointment - Location:  Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The Role The Faculty of Science and Engineering is currently seeking a suitably qualified Senior Scientific Officer, to provide technical and operational support across research and teaching laboratory facilities and activities within Applied BioSciences and the School of Natural Sciences. As the successful applicant, you will be actively engaged in ensuring the smooth and efficient operation of research and teaching laboratories through the provision of high-quality technical support. This includes coordination of the day-to-day technical operational requirements across shared research laboratories, assessing user needs, providing training on and scheduling usage of equipment and facilities, whilst ensuring the laboratories remain safe, functional, and compliant. You will also provide technical support to undergraduate teaching. You will have the opportunity to utilise your working knowledge of both general and specialist equipment as well as health and safety by developing and implementing standard operating procedures (SOP’s) and protocols. You will be a skilled communicator, being able to communicate to a diverse range of users and stake holders. The successful incumbent will be able to work independently and have an aptitude for trouble shooting and problem-solving day to day operational and equipment issues. About You You will have completed a degree in Biology or in a closely related discipline. You will have a sound understanding of relevant compliance regulations including PC2 and OGTR. You have excellent problem-solving skills especially in relation to technical issues. You are able to work with minimal supervision and are hands-on. You have a passion for workplace health and safety with an ability to identify and manage hazards in the workplace. You are an excellent communicator with a proactive nature and are flexible and resilient in your approach. You are agile and manage time and resources effectively to prioritise and deal with issues as they arise. About Us The Faculty of Science and Engineering offers both undergraduate and postgraduate degree programs across a diverse range of disciplines and is home to several world-class research centres and facilities. It is comprised of two research departments and four schools, each with a different scale and/or discipline-specific approach to administration, technical and infrastructure support for research and teaching. The Technical Operations team provide specialised technical support services to teaching and research activities of the Faculty. The team covers a broad range of capabilities and expertise across laboratory, specialist facilities and field-based activities that are essential for the smooth functioning of teaching and research within the Faculty. To Apply To be considered for this position, applicants must respond to the selection criteria below, and attach this as a separate document in the application process with their curriculum vitae.   Essential A degree in Biology or a closely related discipline, or an equivalent combination of education, training, and relevant experience. Demonstrated experience operating and maintaining laboratory facilities and associated equipment, including troubleshooting and resolving a broad range of technical issues. Demonstrated experience working in PC2 facilities, with a strong understanding and practical application of work health and safety legislation, regulations, and safe work practices within biological research laboratory environments. Strong communication and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to communicate effectively in both written and verbal forms. Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities, organise workload effectively, and achieve work objectives within required timeframes. Desirables Demonstrated experience working with controlled environments. Role Enquiries and position description:   Nick Harris, Technical Team Lead via e-mail on nick.harris@mq.edu.au . Applications Close: Sunday 18th of October 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST). Please note that applications for this position are only being accepted from Australian citizens, permanent residents, and those currently residing in Australia with full working rights. We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. This position requires a criminal history check. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . Pre-Employment Checks  Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 28/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
