    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Visa--Relocation-and-Global-Mobility-Specialist_R000024665-1": {
      "title": "Visa, Relocation and Global Mobility Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Talent Acquisition Consultant (Visa and Relocation) delivers high quality end to end services and support to managers particularly in the recruitment of positions where the expected applicant is overseas or interstate. Salary $125K - $140K per annum plus 17% superannuation Full-time continuing appointment Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Open the door for global talent – specialist immigration expertise that brings the world's best minds to Macquarie Every year, academics, researchers, clinicians and professional staff from around the world choose to build their careers at Macquarie University. Behind each of those arrivals sits a visa pathway to navigate, a nomination to lodge, a family to settle and a compliance obligation to meet. This is where you come in. As our Visa, Relocation and Global Mobility Specialist, you will be the University's subject matter expert on immigration and mobility. You will advise hiring managers, faculty leadership and candidates on visa options and eligibility, manage the end-to-end visa lifecycle for international academics and researchers, and coordinate relocation arrangements that help new starters and their families settle in quickly. You will also safeguard the University's compliance position, maintaining sponsorship records, monitoring visa expiries and keeping us audit-ready. Sitting within the Talent Acquisition team in Human Resources, this is a rare specialist role in a complex, highly regulated environment where your advice has visible impact on individual careers, on research programs, and on Macquarie's ability to attract the best talent globally. If you enjoy untangling intricate immigration matters and translating legislation into clear, practical guidance, you will find plenty of scope here. About the Role Reporting to the Head of Talent Acquisition, you will provide specialist, high-level guidance, information, compliance oversight and reporting on immigration and relocation matters to internal stakeholders, current staff, prospective staff and international visitors. Your responsibilities will include: Providing expert advice to hiring managers and University leaders on visa and immigration regulations, compliance and reporting Assessing visa eligibility, explaining visa subclasses (including 407, 408, 482 and 186) and outlining step-by-step processes for existing staff, prospective employees and visiting academics Managing the visa lifecycle for distinguished researchers and postdoctoral fellows, including employer nomination processing and correspondence with government departments Applying and upholding the University's immigration policies and procedures, mitigating risk across all cases and escalating any breaches Maintaining mandatory sponsorship records, tracking visa expiry dates and work right compliance and ensuring readiness for federal immigration audits Acting as the primary contact point between the University, external legal counsel and government departments, and liaising with external agencies to resolve issues as they arise Coordinating international and domestic relocation benefits, housing resources and onboarding logistics for incoming staff and their families Delivering information sessions and training to HR colleagues and stakeholders across the organisation on immigration changes, compliance, visa sponsorship and policy adherence About Us Human Resources sits within the portfolio of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor People and Operations, delivering high-level strategic advisory services to Macquarie University and its entities including Macquarie University Hospital and Health Clinics, and U@MQ, the University's commercial enterprise. Our HR Business Partnering teams and Centres of Expertise span Employee Relations, Talent Acquisition, Remuneration, and Capability, Culture and Inclusion, with HR Shared Services and HR Applications underpinning the portfolio. The Talent Acquisition team is the specialist function responsible for attracting and acquiring domestic and international talent across the University and its entities. Our work is guided by Macquarie's values: collective ambition, purposeful collaboration, bold innovation and genuine care. About You (Selection Criteria) You are an immigration and mobility specialist who reads legislation closely, keeps meticulous records and explains complex requirements in plain language. You navigate large organisations with ease, handle sensitive personal information with discretion, and find practical solutions when a case does not fit the standard pathway. Qualifications in HR, business, law or a related discipline and/or substantial relevant experience; OMARA registration desirable Demonstrated experience in immigration consulting, corporate mobility or global relocation, ideally within a university, large public sector institution or comparable regulated environment Detailed knowledge of Australian immigration legislation and visa processes, including visa subclasses 407, 408, 482 and 186, academic exemptions and pathways relevant to research and higher education Proven expertise in employer-sponsored visas, nomination processing and immigration compliance, with the capability to interpret and apply migration legislation autonomously within a complex organisational context High-level stakeholder engagement skills, including liaison with government agencies, external legal counsel and senior University stakeholders, along with discretion in handling personal data Well-developed case management skills, exceptional attention to detail, and the capacity to organise multiple priorities within tight timelines Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including experience delivering information sessions or training on compliance-related matters How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applications Close: 18 October 2026 We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact Sarah Bate, Head of Talent Acquisition at sarah.bate@mq.edu.au Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. This role requires a criminal history check. Australian citizenship or full working rights in Australia are required. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Deputy-Dean--Education-and-Employability_R000024453-1": {
      "title": "Deputy Dean, Education and Employability",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nLead the Faculty of Science and Engineering's education strategy, lifting teaching standards and student and graduate outcomes. Macquarie University has partnered with Orchard Talent Group in this executive search. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role, please contact Phil Graham, Partner or Jess Young, Researcher at macquarie@orchardtalent.com.au.                                              To be considered, please forward a copy of your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (found in the Digital Candidate Brochure, linked below) to macquarie@orchardtalent.com.au. https://www.mq.edu.au/about/about-the-university/jobs-at-macquarie/deputy-dean-of-education-and-employability-fse?FORCE_BACKUP_LOGIN=1 The organisation The Faculty of Science and Engineering is home to more than 600 staff and over 7,000 coursework and graduate students, with a strong commitment to delivering an exceptional student experience and preparing graduates for the future of work. As one of Macquarie University’s largest faculties, we bring together leading educators, researchers and industry partners to deliver innovative, high-quality education across science, technology, engineering and related disciplines. Our approach to education is grounded in real-world learning, interdisciplinary collaboration and strong connections with industry, government and the broader community. Alongside our internationally recognised research and innovation, these partnerships create opportunities for students to develop the technical expertise, professional capabilities and networks they need to succeed in a dynamic employment landscape and make a positive impact locally, nationally and globally.   The opportunity Reporting to the Executive Dean, you will drive the development and delivery of the faculty's learning and teaching plans, educational activities and teaching quality. As a driving force behind implementation of the Our Education pillar of the FSE Strategy 2026–2030, you will turn its priorities into tangible actions and results by leading initiatives that raise teaching standards, enrich the student experience and strengthen graduate outcomes.  As a member of the Faculty Executive, you will build strong, collaborative relationships with Heads of School and Research Departments, Directors of Education, Course Directors, fellow Deputy Deans, Associate Deans, and Deputy Vice-Chancellor and Vice-President portfolios, working together to advance the University's educational mission and elevate the student experience and graduate employability. Specifically, you will: drive the development and delivery of the faculty's learning and teaching plans, educational activities and teaching quality lead implementation of the Our Education pillar of the FSE Strategy 2026–2030, turning priorities into tangible actions and results lead initiatives that raise teaching standards, enrich the student experience and strengthen graduate outcomes build strong, collaborative relationships with Heads of School and Research Departments, Directors of Education, Course Directors, fellow Deputy Deans, Associate Deans, and Deputy Vice-Chancellor and Vice-President portfolios work together to advance the University's educational mission and elevate the student experience and graduate employability.   About you You are a senior academic leader with a deep understanding of undergraduate and postgraduate education and a genuine commitment to student outcomes in a STEM environment. You bring a clear vision for the future of education and the proven ability to turn that vision into strategy and initiatives that make a real difference for diverse student cohorts.  Your credibility is built on an outstanding record in teaching and research. You pair this with real strategic delivery: identifying, building and sustaining effective relationships with internal and external stakeholders, and using superior negotiation and influencing skills to bring people together and move an agenda forward.  Above all, you are a collegial and inspiring leader. You mentor teams to achieve strategic and operational goals, contribute actively to building the institution, and nurture positive, collaborative relationships with faculty and institutional colleagues.    How to Apply Macquarie University has partnered with Orchard Talent Group in this executive search. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role, please contact Phil Graham, Partner or Jess Young, Researcher at macquarie@orchardtalent.com.au.                                              To be considered, please forward a copy of your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (found in the Digital Candidate Brochure, linked below) to macquarie@orchardtalent.com.au. Applications Close: Sunday, 18 October 2026 Link to Digital Candidate Brochure: https://www.mq.edu.au/about/about-the-university/jobs-at-macquarie/deputy-dean-of-education-and-employability-fse   If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Group-Fitness-Instructor_R000024623": {
      "title": "Group Fitness Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nDeliver engaging group fitness classes, leading choreographed or freestyle programs, demonstrating exercises and correcting technique to ensure a safe, enjoyable experience. The Role Are you passionate about fitness and love leading energising, high-quality group workouts? We're looking for enthusiastic Group Fitness Instructors to bring their energy to our vibrant fitness community. Whether you're an experienced instructor or just starting your Group Fitness career, we're looking for people who can connect with members, bring positive energy and are keen to learn and develop. We offer a diverse range of classes, including Les Mills programs, freestyle formats and Reformer Pilates. Whether you're delivering high-energy workouts or mindful movement-based sessions, you'll play a key role in creating an engaging and motivating experience for our members. For equipment-based classes, you'll also have access to Les Mills Smart Tech equipment . What You'll Do Deliver engaging and professional Group Fitness classes Lead with confidence, demonstrating safe and effective techniques Provide high-level coaching to suit all fitness levels and abilities Foster a welcoming, inclusive atmosphere where members feel supported Build rapport with participants and contribute to positive member experiences Play a role in promoting classes and gym events What We're Looking For A genuine passion for Group Fitness and creating great member experiences — we value attitude, energy and potential as much as experience Confident, positive and engaging communication skills A willingness to learn, take feedback and continue developing as an instructor A team-first attitude and enthusiasm for contributing to our fitness community Current relevant fitness qualification/registration, First Aid and CPR Valid Working with Children Check Relevant program accreditation where required Desirable programs: Les Mills Shapes, Reformer Pilates, Aqua Aerobics, Les Mills Bodypump Heavy and Zumba Availability across a range of class times, with early mornings and lunchtimes preferred Applicants must have the right to work in Australia. About Us Based on the Macquarie University Campus, the centre is a multipurpose fitness venue featuring a fully equipped Health Club, an indoor and outdoor heated pool, Group Fitness classes, and a variety of social sport programs. Programs run seven days a week and incorporate participation from the broader community as well as university members. Benefits of working for Campus Life Join a supportive, inclusive and vibrant team Instruct participants from the broader community as well as university members and students Be involved in member engagement events, launches and on-campus staff and student activations Complimentary gym membership to Macquarie University Sport & Aquatics Centre Access to Macquarie University Library (borrowing, printing, computer access and databases) Access to the employee flu shot program through the University How to apply Click APPLY and include your resume and a short cover letter telling us about yourself, the programs you're qualified or interested in teaching, your availability, and why you'd like to join our Group Fitness team. Please contact Katrina Shaw (Fitness Services Coordinator) at katrina.shaw@mq.edu.au if you have any specific questions regarding this position. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 13/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Early-Childhood-Road-Safety-Education-Consultant_R000024644": {
      "title": "Early Childhood Road Safety Education Consultant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n- Salary Package: Competitive salary plus 12% super - Appointment Type: Full-time (37.5 hours per week), fixed-term appointment until December 2027. - Location: Kids and Traffic Program | Macquarie University Services Limited (MQSL) | (Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Are you an experienced Early Childhood Teacher with a passion for professional learning, community engagement, and making a meaningful difference? Do you enjoy working collaboratively with educators and leading initiatives that support positive outcomes for children? Are you looking for a new opportunity in the ECEC sector? The Kids and Traffic Early Childhood Road Safety Education Program is seeking an enthusiastic and capable Early Childhood Road Safety Education Consultant to deliver professional development, provide expert advice, and support education and care services across NSW to implement best-practice road safety education. About the Role You will work with educators, service leaders, families, tertiary institutions, and community stakeholders to promote high-quality road safety education for young children. Through workshops, tailored support, community projects, and stakeholder engagement, you will contribute to improved road safety outcomes for children and families across NSW. This is an exciting opportunity to combine your early childhood expertise with adult learning and community engagement while contributing to a well-established statewide program. The Kids and Traffic Program is funded as a partnership between Transport for NSW and Macquarie University. The role is initially available from 1st February 2027 to December 2027 . Further employment may be available depending on funding. Key Responsibilities Develop, deliver and coordinate professional development workshops for early childhood education and care services, outside school hours care services, and tertiary education providers. Provide tailored road safety education support, leadership, and expert advice to the early childhood sector. Build and maintain strong relationships with educators, service leaders, and community stakeholders. Lead and support community-based projects that address local road safety issues and improve outcomes for children and families. Contribute to resource development, program initiatives, and team projects. Support the effective operation and success of the Kids and Traffic Program through ongoing administration and stakeholder engagement activities.   Why Join Kids and Traffic ? Kids and Traffic is the leading provider of early childhood road safety education in NSW. The Program is in its fourth decade of a shared governance partnership between Transport for NSW, Macquarie University, the NSW Department of Education, Catholic Schools NSW, and Independent Schools NSW. Working within a respected statewide program, you'll have the opportunity to: Engage with educators and communities across NSW Work with a highly regarded team of education professionals Apply your teaching expertise in a unique and rewarding specialist role. Make a positive impact on children's safety and wellbeing. About You You are a motivated and experienced early childhood professional who enjoys supporting others to achieve best practice. You have excellent communication skills, strong initiative, and the ability to build productive relationships across diverse communities and settings.   Key Selection Criteria Four-year Early Childhood Education degree, or equivalent ACECQA approved teaching qualification, Demonstrated success in teaching and leading people and programs in early childhood education and care services, Strong understanding of the diversity of early childhood education and care settings and current sector influences, Proven ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team, Experience initiating and implementing projects with minimal supervision, Highly developed written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, Proficiency in Microsoft 365 applications and the ability to use digital technology to support teaching and learning, and Ability to think creatively and develop practical strategies for young children, families, and educators. In addition, a Certificate IV in Training and Assessment or a willingness to obtain is desirable. Other Role Requirements Ability to travel throughout Greater Sydney and regional NSW, including overnight travel, evening workshops, and weekend work when and as required. Current unrestricted NSW Driver Licence. Current Working with Children Check. Note: The successful applicant will be required to complete a medical assessment, demerit point check and a Police Check.   Apply Now To be considered for this position, please apply online and make sure to include a copy of your CV along with a cover letter addressing the essential criteria above, Applicants must be legally entitled to work in Australia and have full work rights for the duration of the appointment.  Applicants are strongly encouraged to contact Louise Cosgrove – Acting Program Director, Kids and Traffic , on 0408283084 or louise.cosgrove@mq.edu.au for further information about the role. For recruitment enquiries, please contact Mirna Alaaidin at mirna.alaaiddin@mq.edu.au   *** Applications for this position will close on Sunday 1st November 2026 @ 11:59 p.m. (AEDT). Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and we reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 01/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Hotel-Front-Office-Receptionist_R000024580": {
      "title": "Hotel Front Office Receptionist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nLakeside Hotel & Conference Centre is seeking a full-time receptionist to join our friendly and professional Front Office team at our North Ryde campus. • Salary Package: $62,830 per annum plus employer's superannuation • Appointment Type: Full time, continuing appointment • Location: Lakeside Hotel & Conference Centre | Macquarie University Services Limited (MQSL) | (Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde This is an exciting opportunity for a hospitality professional who enjoys working in a dynamic environment, delivering exceptional guest experiences and being involved in a broad range of hotel operations. About the Role As a receptionist, you will be one of the first points of contact for our guests and clients. You will play an important role in ensuring every guest receives a warm welcome, professional service and a positive experience throughout their stay. Your responsibilities will include: Provide a warm, professional and welcoming experience to all guests, visitors and clients. Manage guest arrivals and departures, including efficient check-in and check-out procedures. Process reservations, amendments, cancellations and guest requests accurately. Respond professionally and promptly to guest enquiries in person, by telephone and via email. Process accommodation, restaurant and other guest payments accurately and in accordance with hotel procedures. Manage cash, EFTPOS and credit card transactions and complete required financial procedures. Maintain accurate guest profiles, reservations, records and documentation within the hotel PMS. Monitor and manage guest requests, ensuring they are followed through to completion. Liaise closely with Housekeeping, Food & Beverage, Functions, Maintenance and other departments to ensure smooth hotel operations. Assist with group bookings, conferences, functions and university-related accommodation requirements. Provide information to guests regarding hotel facilities, services, local attractions and transportation. Handle guest feedback and complaints professionally, escalating matters where appropriate and following through to resolution. Identify opportunities to enhance the guest experience and support repeat business. Maintain a high standard of presentation, professionalism and customer service at all times. Follow hotel policies, procedures and operational standards. Complete daily Front Office procedures, reports and administrative tasks accurately. Support night audit and financial reconciliation processes where required. Ensure appropriate security, emergency, WH&S and risk-management procedures are followed. Assist with general hotel operations and other reasonable duties as required. ABOUT YOU You are someone who believes the core of hospitality is customer service and possess a friendly and approachable manner. You are great at multi-tasking, have excellent verbal and written communication skills and can think on your feet to solve problems. To be successful in this role, you will have: Demonstrated experience in a customer-facing or customer-service role (experience in hospitality or a related service industry is preferred). A genuine commitment to excellent customer service and the ability to remain calm and resolve problems in challenging situations. Strong organisational, time-management and attention-to-detail skills, including the ability to maintain accurate records and manage competing priorities. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. The ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team. Experience handling cash, EFTPOS, credit card transactions and daily financial reconciliation. Proficient in the use of the Microsoft Office Suite of programs; experience using Opera Cloud PMS or another hotel property management system is highly regarded. Previous hotel Front Office or Reception experience, including knowledge of reservations, check-in/check-out and Front Office procedures, as well as experience in a conference, events or functions environment is highly desirable. *** The successful candidate must hold a current NSW Responsible Service of Alcohol (RSA) competency card and unrestricted full work rights in Australia, and will be required to undergo a police check. Please note: This role requires the ability to work across AM, PM, weekend and occasional night shifts. Full flexibility is essential. ABOUT US Lakeside Hotel and Conference Centre is an award-winning venue situated on the picturesque grounds of Macquarie University at North Ryde. The facility supports both University and non-University business and offers a diverse range of hospitality services, including an award-winning 4-star hotel, licensed bar, contemporary à la carte restaurant – Lachlan’s, café and multipurpose function and conference facilities. Benefits of Working for Lakeside Hotel & Conference Centre This is an excellent opportunity to join a professional hospitality team within a unique university-based environment. You will have the opportunity to work across hotel accommodation, conferences, events, food and beverage and university-related business, providing a varied and rewarding hospitality experience. In addition to this, our benefits include: Complementary Macquarie University Sport & Aquatic Centre gym access Staff discounts at Campus Life operated hospitality and retail outlets Ongoing development and mentoring opportunities Generous leave entitlements Access to our staff wellbeing program and staff support services Working on a vibrant parkland campus, with a huge variety of food & beverage outlets, and general practice & hospital amenities Access to discounted corporate health insurance and free employee flu shot program. Subsidised onsite parking options How to Apply If you are ready to deliver outstanding guest experiences and join a supportive team, APPLY NOW with your CV and cover letter addressing your suitability against the role requirements/ criteria above as part of the online application process. For role-specific queries , contact Saad Khan, Hotel Front Office Manager at s.khan@mq.edu.au . Applications Close: Sunday 18 October 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEST) If you require any support or reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, please let us know. Note:  Applications will be reviewed as they are received and we reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the closing date, and/or remove the advert earlier than originally advertised, so early applications are encouraged. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Payroll-Governance-Specialist_R000024668": {
      "title": "Payroll Governance Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $147,124 – $155,386 (HEW 9) p.a, plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading  - Appointment Type:  Full-time, 2-year fixed term role  - Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde  Strengthen payroll governance, safeguard compliance and help deliver accurate pay outcomes for thousands of staff   As our Payroll Governance Specialist, you will be the subject matter expert on payroll legislation, compliance and controls within our Human Resources Shared Services team. You will provide expert advice, guide audit and assurance activity, and identify practical opportunities to strengthen payroll risk management and operational effectiveness across the Macquarie University Group.  This is a specialist role with genuine organisational reach. You will work across HR, Finance, IT and faculty operations teams, as well as with internal and external auditors, government agencies and State Revenue Offices, contributing to projects and initiatives that improve how payroll governance is designed and delivered. If you enjoy detailed, high-stakes work where accuracy has a direct and visible impact on people's lives, this role offers that in abundance.  About the Role Reporting to the Manager, Payroll Services, you will be accountable for the integrity, compliance, governance and continuous improvement of payroll processes and controls. Your responsibilities will include: Working in partnership with the Manager, Payroll Services, Group Finance and other key stakeholders so payroll processes and controls uphold financial integrity, statutory reporting requirements, audit obligations and organisational risk management objectives.  Ensuring all payroll controls are executed in line with the Payroll Governance Framework.  Confirming payroll operations comply with relevant enterprise agreements, modern awards, employment legislation, taxation obligations, and University policies and procedures.  Verifying that systems are accurately configured and that appropriate access is maintained in accordance with payroll controls (for example Dayforce aPay, Workday, Kronos, document management and banking applications).  Reviewing payroll controls, processes and governance practices on a regular basis to identify risks, progress continuous improvement, and enhance compliance and control effectiveness.  Coordinating internal and external audit activities, including providing information to auditors, reviewing draft audit recommendations and ensuring audit management actions are completed by their due dates.  Preparing regular payroll reports for internal and external stakeholders, including the Audit & Risk Committee and Payroll Governance Committees.  Managing and contributing to payroll projects and governance initiatives, including wage remediation activities encompassing data analysis, root cause analysis, reconciliation calculations, change management, stakeholder communications and process improvement.  Reviewing customer and service performance data to identify trends and opportunities for improvement.  Assisting the Manager, Payroll Services and the wider Payroll Services team with strategic and complex operational matters as required.  About Us This role sits within the Deputy Vice-Chancellor, People and Operations portfolio, which provides executive leadership of Professional Services across the Macquarie University Group. The Shared Services function delivers first-class services to our students and staff, encompassing Admissions & Scholarships, Student Shared Services, Enabling Services, and Corporate Shared Services for Finance, IT and HR. Shared Services is built on solid disciplines including service management, continuous improvement, automation and analytics — and, at its heart, a service culture that enables all staff to deliver optimal outcomes for our customers.  About You   You are an experienced payroll professional who is energised by complexity, detail and getting things right. You understand how governance frameworks, controls and legislation come together in a high-volume payroll environment, and you can translate technical requirements into practical improvements that colleagues across the organisation can adopt. You communicate clearly with auditors, executives and employees alike, and you bring a service mindset to every interaction. Experience applying AI and other emerging technologies to improve payroll control management and operations will be viewed favourably.  Selection Criteria   Relevant tertiary qualifications in business, accounting, human resources or a related discipline, and/or an equivalent combination of education and experience in a payroll specialist position.  Demonstrated experience in complex, high-volume payroll operations involving a diverse range of modern awards and enterprise agreements.  Demonstrated experience establishing, managing and improving payroll governance, controls, risk and assurance frameworks, including managing payroll control and compliance reviews and audits.  Well-developed knowledge of, and demonstrated experience in, compliance with employment legislation and employer obligations including enterprise agreements, modern awards, superannuation, PAYG, payroll tax, Single Touch Payroll and workers compensation.  Demonstrated experience contributing to wage remediation activities and complex payroll calculations, with a high level of accuracy, attention to detail and focus on customer service.  Well-developed problem-solving skills, with the ability to interpret data and insights to improve performance and service outcomes.  Sound technical skills including demonstrated experience using complex HR/Payroll systems (experience with Dayforce aPay and Workday is highly regarded), together with effective stakeholder engagement and communication skills that build productive relationships internally and externally.  How to Apply    To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above).   Applications Close: Sunday 18 th  of October 2026 at 11:59 pm (AEST). We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date.  Applicants must have valid Australian Working Rights. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact TA Consultant Kate Wiliams -  k.williams@mq.edu.au .  Why Join Us?  Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today .  We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University.         Flexible, hybrid work arrangements   17% Superannuation   Subsidised onsite parking options   Extensive training and professional development programs   Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents   Onsite vacation care during school holidays   Discounted health insurance   Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre   Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support   Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics   Pre-Employment Checks    Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow---Research-Fellow----Management-Organisational-Psychology_R000024594": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow / Research Fellow -  Management/Organisational Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n• Annual Salary Package: Level A - Post Doctoral Fellow ($89,579 - $120,621) plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading, OR, Level B - Research Fellow ($127,138 - $150,425) plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading. Pro-rata rates apply for part-time appointments. • Full-time or part-time, fixed-term position for 2 years. • Hybrid role - Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The Macquarie University Health at Work Research Centre is expanding its research team and has an exciting opportunity for a talented, highly motivated researcher who is keen to apply and further develop their expertise. About the role In this position, you will contribute to funded industry projects focused on work design and wellbeing at work. Working closely with the Centre Director, you’ll apply your research expertise to collaborative projects that aim to improve health and wellbeing in organisations and translate research into practical outcomes. About us Since its foundation in 1964, Macquarie University has engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. The Health at Work Research Centre is part of Macquarie Business School , the University’s focal point for business, management and economics research and education. The Health at Work Research Centre conducts pioneering research to improve health and wellbeing at work and to advance health services through research and industry collaboration. The Centre investigates the complex interplay of factors that advance health and wellness, develops effective interventions and translates knowledge into policy and practice. Our interdisciplinary research unit uses multi-method collaborative research to improve health and social outcomes aimed at optimising the health of people in organisations and the design and management of health and social care. Macquarie University Health at Work Research Centre About You You’re a motivated researcher with a PhD in a relevant discipline and a developing or established research track record in organisational behaviour, HR, organisational psychology or a related field. You bring strong analytical and communication skills, enjoy working with research partners, and are keen to apply and grow your expertise in the Australian context. Essential Selection Criteria (Academic Level A & B) A PhD in a relevant discipline (e.g. organisational psychology, management or other relevant business discipline, health services research) Peer-reviewed publications. Research experience in organisational behavior, HR or organisational psychology or similar interventions undertaken in the Australian context. Experience in preparing human research ethics applications. Demonstrable skills in the analysis of quantitative and qualitative data analysis software. Excellent oral and written communication skills, experience conducting systematic reviews and external stakeholder reports. Demonstrated capacity to work independently and collaboratively with internal and/or external partners. Criteria for Research Fellow - Academic Level B (in addition to essential criteria above) Track record in managing research projects and a small research team. Experience in preparing and securing research grants. Track record of leading research publications, presentations and external stakeholder liaison. *** The successful candidate will be required to complete a Police Check and an academic qualification check. How to Apply To be considered for this position, please apply online by submitting your CV and a separate cover letter (not exceeding 3 pages) that demonstrates how you meet the following selection criteria above. Specific Role Enquires: Professor Rebecca Mitchell at rebecca.mitchell@mq.edu.au APPLICATIONS CLOSE: Sunday 18 October 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEST) Note: The successful applicant must have valid work rights in Australia for the duration of the appointment. *** We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. Why Join Us? We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Our prime location is just a short walk from Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Shopping Centre. Enjoy the benefits of working at a campus that offers: 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Flexible working options Training and professional development Onsite childcare facilities Discounted health insurance (Medibank) Onsite vacation care Employee Assistance Program Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Manager--Positions---Appointments_R000024670-1": {
      "title": "Manager, Positions & Appointments",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $126,306– $140,543 per annum plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading  - Full-time, continuing role, 35 hours per week  - Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde (hybrid working arrangement)  Shape the experience of each new starter at Macquarie   Every new role created and every person appointed at Macquarie University begins with the work of the Positions and Appointments Team. As Manager, Positions and Appointments, you will lead the service that makes position establishment, appointments and onboarding accurate, timely and easy to navigate for staff and leaders across the Macquarie University Group.  You will join a HR Shared Services function that values end-to-end thinking and continuous improvement, working alongside stakeholders across a diverse and complex university group. It is an opportunity to bring service design, systems know-how and team leadership together in one role, with real scope to shape how things are done. This is a role for someone who enjoys the full picture: the people, the process and the technology. You will guide a capable team, refine the way services are designed and delivered, and make sure the data and systems underpinning them are reliable. Your work will be visible in dashboards that inform planning, in processes that remove friction, and in the excellent customer service experienced  by each new starter.  About the Role   Reporting to the Head of HR Shared Services, you will be accountable for the delivery and continuous improvement of position establishment and appointment services. Your responsibilities will include: Lead the delivery and continuous improvement of position establishment and appointment services, working with key stakeholders to provide efficient, effective support and a positive staff experience  Build and manage an effective team, including work allocation, capability development and performance management, to maintain high levels of engagement and motivation  Provide operational oversight of HR services relating to position establishment and employee appointments, escalating issues and risks to inform decision-making and planning  Plan and manage the use of agreed processes, standards, methods and tools to underpin efficiency, effectiveness, reliability and consistency of service delivery and performance  Maintain high data quality and optimising data to improve client visibility and decision-making through reports and dashboards  Manage and optimise the technology solutions that enable service delivery, including requirement definition and testing of changes and upgrades  Develop long-term customer relationships and maintain a clear understanding of customer needs, balancing competing internal and external stakeholder demands to deliver operational excellence and a high level of customer satisfaction  Lead ongoing analysis and review of HR services and processes to identify opportunities for value optimisation, improvement and enhancement, informed by customer data and service performance metrics  Develop service performance standards and reporting against performance metrics aligned with business and HR objectives, while fostering a work environment with a culture of accountability  About Us   Macquarie University is a place where interesting people come to do their best work. Our Human Resources Shared Services function supports HR execution across the University Group including Macquarie University, U@MQ and Macquarie University Health and delivers services that are accurate, responsive and human-centred. The Positions and Appointments team sits at the heart of this, enabling the establishment of roles and the appointment of people who make our teaching, research and professional services possible.  About You   You are an experienced HR operations or HR shared services professional who understands process and systems as well as people. You are comfortable owning a service end to end from how a process is designed, to how it is configured in the technology, to how it is tested, measured and improved. You bring clarity to complexity, and you enjoy building teams that take pride in getting the detail right.  Selection Criteria   Demonstrated experience leading and developing a team delivering HR operations, shared services or transactional HR services in a complex organisation  Proven experience in position establishment, appointments, onboarding or related employee lifecycle services, including operational oversight and risk escalation  Technical competency with HRIS or workflow technology ( Workday or equivalent), including requirement definition, configuration input, testing of changes and upgrades  Demonstrated capability in process and systems design, with a track record of end-to-end service improvement informed by data and performance metrics  Experience establishing service performance standards, reporting against metrics, and maintaining high standards of data quality to enable reporting and dashboards  Well-developed stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to manage expectations and competing priorities across internal and external customers  Sound working knowledge of relevant employment frameworks, EEO and WHS obligations, and their practical application in HR service delivery  How to Apply   To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above).  Applications Close: Sunday 18th of October 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST).   We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date.   Applicants must have valid Australian Working Rights.   For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact TA Consultant Kate Wiliams -  k.williams@mq.edu.au . Why Join Us?   Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today .  We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University.    Flexible, hybrid work arrangements  17% Superannuation  Subsidised onsite parking options  Extensive training and professional development programs  Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents  Onsite vacation care during school holidays  Discounted health insurance  Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre  Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support  Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics  Pre-Employment Checks   Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Research-Fellow---Machine-Learning-for-LEO-Satellite-Communications_R000024614": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Machine Learning for LEO Satellite Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n- Salary Package: $112,550 - $120,621 (Level A6-A8) per annum, plus 17% employer’s superannuation and annual leave loading. Appointment will be commensurate with qualifications, experience and research track record - Appointment Type: Full-time (35 hours per week), fixed-term appointment for 2 years, with a possibility of further renewal subject to funding - Location: Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The Role Macquarie University’s School of Engineering is seeking a Research Fellow to help develop the next generation of intelligent, self-organising satellite networks. The position contributes to “Brain-in-Space: A Machine Learning Framework for Self-Organizing Low-Earth Orbit Satellite Networks”, funded by the Global Science and Technology Diplomacy Fund. You will investigate how low Earth orbit (LEO) satellites can operate as intelligent agents, learning to make decisions and coordinate their actions as orbital and traffic conditions change. Your research will combine machine learning, mathematical modelling and algorithm design to enable autonomous operation of large satellite constellations. You will also develop an open-source simulation and benchmarking platform to evaluate these methods under realistic network conditions. You will work closely with Dr Hazer Inaltekin at Macquarie University and international collaborators including Associate Professor Wonjae Shin at Korea University, Professor Jungwoo Lee at Seoul National University, and Professor Vincent Poor at Princeton University. Within the project’s objectives, you will have considerable scope to shape the research direction, develop your own ideas and lead research contributions. The role offers opportunities to publish in leading journals and conferences, contribute to postgraduate supervision, and build your research profile through international collaboration. You will also contribute to technical reporting and collaborative research activities across the project team. Selection Criteria: Essential: A PhD in electrical and electronic engineering, computer science, applied mathematics, or a related discipline. A strong research publication record in relevant international journals and conferences, commensurate with career stage. Strong mathematical and algorithmic capability, with demonstrated experience applying machine learning to research problems Strong programming skills in Python and/or MATLAB Strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated ability to plan and manage research activities independently, prioritise tasks and meet project deadlines Commitment to collaborative research and teamwork Desirable: Knowledge of information theory and communication theory relevant to wireless communication systems Prior research experience in satellite communications or              networking, particularly low Earth orbit (LEO) systems Experience applying machine learning to sequential decision-making or multi-agent coordination Experience developing, validating and documenting research simulation software Interest in and ability to contribute to the supervision and mentoring of postgraduate research students   Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . How to Apply To be considered for this role, please submit:   Up to date Resume, including the publication list A Cover Letter addressing the above selection criteria (not exceeding 2 pages) Up to date Referees Role specific enquiries:  Dr Hazer Inaltekin at hazer.inaltekin@mq.edu.au . Applications Close:  Friday 30th of October 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST). International applicants are encouraged to apply.  VISA sponsorship available for the successful candidate, subject to eligibility. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 30/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Early-Childhood-Teacher_R000024731": {
      "title": "Early Childhood Teacher",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nInspire curiosity, nurture a lifelong love of learning, and help shape children’s earliest years on a vibrant University campus. · Competitive annual salary plus super · 1 full-time, continuing position · Banksia Cottage, U@MQ Ltd — Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Do you believe the early years are a unique and valuable time in a child’s life? At Banksia Cottage, one of Campus Life’s early learning centres on Macquarie University’s campus, you’ll help lead a team in delivering a high-quality, inclusive early learning program. You’ll be part of a welcoming community where children’s wellbeing, relationships and professional learning are valued. About the Role We’re looking for an Early Childhood Teacher to join the team at Banksia Cottage. Reporting to the Centre Manager, you’ll be an advocate for children and work with the room team to develop, implement and evaluate a high-quality educational program. You’ll bring a strong understanding of child development, a commitment to inclusive practice, and the confidence to support a team. You’ll also undertake Room Leader and Responsible Person duties as required. Your key responsibilities include: Developing, implementing and evaluating the educational program, including maintaining developmental records. Applying your knowledge of child development to support children’s learning and wellbeing. Interacting positively and respectfully with children and families. Working collaboratively within a large and diverse team. Maintaining current knowledge of the Early Years Learning Framework and National Quality Standards. Supporting diversity, equity and inclusion activities. Contributing to professional development and continuous improvement. Supervising a small team and supporting team performance, with guidance from the Centre Manager. Undertaking Room Leader and Responsible Person duties as required. Following approved policies and procedures to help keep children safe, including those relating to child protection, supervision, health and wellbeing. You’ll also enjoy a range of benefits, including: Education and professional development opportunities Paid lunch breaks, with no requirement to remain on the premises Paid staff meetings and generous release time Free access to the Macquarie University Sport & Aquatic Centre Additional paid concessional days Staff wellbeing and support services, including an employee flu vaccination program Discounted corporate health insurance Bonus discounts and reward points at Campus Life outlets About Us U@MQ Ltd is a not-for-profit controlled entity of Macquarie University, known as Campus Life. Located at Macquarie University’s Wallumattagal Campus in North Ryde, Campus Life operates four early learning centres providing high-quality education for children from six weeks of age, as well as a vacation care program for primary school-aged children. Banksia Cottage is one of these centres. Its philosophy recognises children as independent people whose rights, identities, voices and choices are encouraged and respected. Play, strong relationships, connection with nature, and a commitment to ongoing learning are central to the centre’s approach. You can read more in the Banksia Cottage Philosophy . Campus Life has access to University spaces and facilities to support and enhance its programs, and collaborates regularly with the University community, including the Macquarie School of Education. We are committed to the safety of children and our people. We embrace diversity, welcome our people as they are, and prioritise professional development. At Campus Life, you’ll be part of a dynamic, committed and supportive team. We share the values of Courage, Agility, Rigour, Empowerment and Support (CARES), and aim to make them visible in our actions and words. About You You’re a passionate early childhood professional who believes in the value of quality early education and the relationships that underpin it. You bring a sound understanding of child development, an inclusive and collaborative approach, and a commitment to children’s safety and wellbeing. You’re confident supporting a team and contributing to a positive learning environment. You will share our organisational values of Courage, Agility, Rigour, Empowerment and Support (CARES) , and demonstrate them through your actions and interactions. Demonstrated experience developing, implementing and evaluating high-quality, inclusive educational programs, with sound knowledge of child development and appropriate strategies for interacting with young children, Previous experience working with children aged 0-5 years in an early learning setting, Demonstrated ability to supervise children effectively, maintain a clean and safe environment, as well as understand child protection laws and responsibilities as a Mandatory Reporter, Experience supervising a team, including coaching and developing staff and providing direction and constructive feedback, Sound knowledge of the National Quality Framework, including the National Law, Regulations, National Quality Standards and Early Years Learning Framework, Understanding of the responsibilities of a Responsible Person, Well-developed interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build respectful and ethical relationships with children, families and colleagues, Computer literacy, including experience with Microsoft Office 365 Qualifications & Specific Requirements The following must be current or completed before commencement: ACECQA-approved degree in early childhood education Current NESA accreditation Approved First Aid qualification and approved Asthma and Anaphylaxis qualification NSW Working with Children Check and a Police Check Food Handling training Current Child Protection training, including a recognised course code for CHCPRT025 – Identify and Report Children and Young People at Risk Current child safety training (Geccko) An Early Learning Prohibition Notice Declaration *** You must have full unrestricted work rights in Australia. How to Apply If you’re passionate about being part of an inclusive, vibrant and team-oriented organisation, we encourage you to apply. Please submit your resume and a cover letter explaining how you meet the selection criteria and requirements above. For general enquiries or a copy of the Position Description, please contact Marina Galstyan on 02 9850 7781, or marina.galstyan@mq.edu.au . If you need support or reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, please let us know so we can provide the support you need. Applications close: Sunday 25 October 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEDT) *** We reserve the right to progress or decline an application before the closing date. Child Safe Commitment Campus Life is committed to the safety, wellbeing and empowerment of all children and young people who participate in our programs, and to protecting them from foreseeable harm. We take all allegations and complaints about children’s safety and wellbeing seriously. Every Campus Life employee has a responsibility to understand their role in keeping children and young people safe and to meet their legal obligations to report child abuse and neglect. Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct and strong integrity. Before an offer of employment is finalised, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role. Employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks to the satisfaction of the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 25/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Project-Manager--Australian-Astronomical-Optics_R000024305": {
      "title": "Project Manager, Australian Astronomical Optics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n$126,306 – $140,543 per annum (HEW Level 8) and 17% superannuation and annual leave loading Full-time, fixed term for 2 Years Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Inspire collaboration across diverse teams, drive projects from concept to delivery, and help shape the technologies powering the next generation of astronomical and space discovery. This isn’t your traditional project management role. Here, your project leadership will help turn ambitious scientific ideas into real-world instruments and technologies that explore our universe.  At Australian Astronomical Optics at Macquarie University (AAO), the projects you manage result in physical and digital instruments that are installed on some of the world's largest telescopes, flown in space applications, and used by researchers to answer questions about the universe. As Project Manager, you will take responsibility for the end-to-end delivery of scientific instrument and technology projects for astronomical observatories, space applications and external clients while ensuring projects are within budget, on schedule and to specification. You will work alongside principal investigators, instrument scientists, and multi-disciplinary teams of mechanical, optical, electronics, control and software engineers, bringing structure, visibility and momentum to work that is often first-of-its-kind. If you’re excited by the opportunity to apply your project management expertise to applied research challenges, and to see your work contribute to scientific discovery, research and real-world outcomes, this is a rare opportunity for you to make a meaningful difference. About the Role Reporting to the Head of Programs and Project Management, AAO, you will plan and deliver complex, multi-disciplinary technical projects from proposal through to handover. Key responsibilities include: Overseeing the delivery of complex instrument, technology and software projects on time, within budget and to specification. Monitoring, tracking and documenting project progress against milestones and budgets, and preparing progress reports for senior management and stakeholders. Researching and developing project plans, schedules, materials and labour budgets for proposals, grant submissions and internal project planning. Consulting with Heads of Section on resource allocation requests and directing staff to undertake project tasks within the agreed resource allocation. Managing client and subcontractor relationships, including meetings, reviews and reports, and managing trade-off analyses across budget, schedule, performance, complexity and development issues. Liaising with vendors and stakeholders on high-value or high-risk procurements, including negotiating and managing client contracts and maintaining documentation for variations to scope, price or schedule. Liaising with University research offices, funding agencies and partners to facilitate project set-up, progression and delivery. Identifying risks and issues early and implementing practical solutions to mitigate them. Coordinating multi-disciplinary teams within a matrix delivery model. Applying and monitoring work health and safety requirements in a lab-based technical environment and complying with relevant EEO and WHS obligations. Contributing to the delivery of AAO’s research-based learning and teaching objectives. Kindly please note that work hours may vary from time to time to accommodate business needs, and national or international travel may be required for project meetings, conferences or events. About Us The Faculty of Science and Engineering is characterised by the spirit of innovation. Here we nurture the next generation of science and technology innovators. The pairing of engineering and science in a single faculty means many of our research discoveries in science see direct technological applications in engineering. Within the faculty, AAO is a research department. Australian Astronomical Optics (AAO) is a recognised world leader in innovative astronomical instrumentation, software and research - designing, building and commissioning advanced instruments for the world's premier observatories. Our expertise spans the development of innovative technologies for astronomical and space instruments, as well as the software and data systems that enable the processing, storage and access of scientific data. We  play a critical role in ensuring these advanced instruments and technologies meet the specifications demanded by world-leading scientific applications, enabling researchers to turn innovative ideas and capabilities into new knowledge and discovery. About You You are an experienced project management professional who is comfortable operating in a technical, research-driven environment. You combine disciplined planning, budgeting and contract management with clear, accessible communication across engineers, scientists, clients and suppliers. Experience in scientific instrumentation, research software, astronomy, space or a comparable technical field is highly regarded, though we welcome applications from candidates with transferable experience from other complex engineering or R&D settings. Selection Criteria Relevant tertiary qualification/s and/or equivalent experience, along with formal project management training (or equivalent experience) and demonstrated ability to adapt and apply methodologies to suit project needs. Demonstrated experience delivering complex, multi-disciplinary technical projects to specification, budget and schedule, including resource planning across a portfolio of projects. Substantial experience across project change, schedule and interdependency, issues, financial, contract, stakeholder, team and workflow management. Highly effective communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to establish and maintain productive relationships with internal and external stakeholders and clients. Knowledge of, or training in, engineering and/or technical development practices for technical instrumentation and research software projects, including a working understanding of relevant technologies, processes and systems engineering approaches. Demonstrated experience coordinating multi-disciplinary teams, contributing to project proposals, and reviewing technical specifications and reports. Significant experience negotiating procurement contracts, together with excellent organisational and time management skills and a working knowledge of health and safety compliance in a lab-based technical environment. Bachelor's degree in engineering, computer science, astronomy, physics, project management, communications or a related discipline (Desirable). How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). To be considered for this position, applicants must have full and unrestricted working rights in Australia. Applications Close: Applications will close on Sunday 25th October at 11.59 PM AEST. Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University: Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 25/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Administration-Coordinator_R000024697": {
      "title": "Administration Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n- Competitive annual salary plus super - Appointment Type: Full time (38 hours), permanent position - Location: Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde, Dharug lan Lead. Improve. Deliver an exceptional customer experience. We’re looking for an experienced Administration Coordinator to join the team at Macquarie University Sport and Aquatic Centre (MUSAC). This is a key leadership role responsible for overseeing administrative operations, financial processes and customer experience outcomes, while leading a small, high-performing team. THE ROLE In this diverse and hands-on role, you will: Oversee and coordinate all financial administration processes, including direct debits, invoicing, billing, debt management and reporting.   Lead, supervise and coach the administration team to build capability and deliver high-quality, consistent service. Support the development and implementation of pricing schedules aligned with business and audit requirements. Manage escalated administrative and customer issues, ensuring timely and effective resolution. Continuously review and improve systems, processes, and procedures to enhance efficiency and customer outcomes. Provide expert guidance on sensitive and confidential administrative matters across the business. Maintain a strong understanding of MUSAC programs, services, fees and terms & conditions. Contribute to Diversity, Equity, Inclusion and Belonging (DEIB) initiatives that support an inclusive and welcoming environment. Ensure compliance with EEO, WHS, and governance requirements.   ABOUT YOU You are a proactive and solutions-focused professional with strong administrative leadership experience. You bring: Relevant tertiary qualification and/or extensive experience in administration, operations, or customer service. Proven experience leading, supervising, and developing high-performing teams. Strong financial administration experience in a complex or membership-based environment. Demonstrated ability to improve processes and drive continuous improvement initiatives. Experience working within governance and compliance frameworks. Strong analytical skills, including experience in data reporting and generating business insights. Excellent communication, organisation, and stakeholder management skills. High attention to detail and the ability to manage competing priorities. Demonstrated skill and experience in Microsoft Office programs including Excel, Word, Outlook and PowerPoint. *** Note: This role requires a criminal history check, as well as a First Aid and CPR certificate. ABOUT US Macquarie University Sport and Aquatic Centre (MUSAC) is a multi-purpose venue offering health, fitness, aquatic, and sporting programs to the university and wider community.  We are committed to creating inclusive, engaging and high-quality experiences for all member and guests. WHY JOIN US? At MUSAC, you’ll join a vibrant and inclusive environment focused on community, wellbeing and excellence. We offer: Complementary Macquarie University Sport & Aquatic Centre gym access  Professional development opportunities Paid concessional days between Christmas and the New Year    Access to staff wellbeing programs  Staff discounts at Campus Life operated hospitality outlets A dynamic and supportive team environment  Working on a beautiful parkland campus Access to discounted corporate health insurance and employee flu shot program Salary sacrifice options  Full access to the University Library  Access to paid parental leave   APPLY NOW If you’re ready to take the next step in your leadership career and make a meaningful impact on customer experience and operational excellence, we’d love to hear from you. Please submit your CV and a cover letter addressing the criteria listed in the About You section via our online application portal. For a confidential discussion, please contact Donna Pearce on 02 9850 7640. If you need any support or reasonable adjustments throughout this recruitment process, please let us know, so we can provide you with the support you need.  APPLICATIONS CLOSE: Wednesday 21 October 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEDT) Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 21/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Early-Childhood-Road-Safety-Education-Workshop-Presenter_R000024716-1": {
      "title": "Early Childhood Road Safety Education Workshop Presenter",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nTo present Kids and Traffic professional development workshops and content regarding road safety education to education and care and related services and their stakeholders. Early Childhood Road Safety Education Workshop Presenter (Casual) Kids and Traffic Program | Macquarie University Services Limited (MQSL) Are you an experienced Early Childhood Teacher who is passionate about supporting educators, children, and families? Do you enjoy facilitating professional learning and inspiring others through education? Are you looking for a new opportunity in the ECEC sector? The Kids and Traffic Early Childhood Road Safety Education Program is seeking an enthusiastic and engaging casual Workshop Presenter to deliver professional development workshops and road safety education content to early childhood education and care services and stakeholders across NSW. About the Role As an Early Childhood Road Safety Education Workshop Presenter, you will deliver high-quality professional development workshops to educators, service leaders, families, tertiary students, and community stakeholders. Workshops are delivered both face-to-face and online, requiring flexibility, initiative, and strong presentation skills. This is an exciting opportunity to combine your early childhood expertise with adult learning and community engagement to make a meaningful contribution to child safety outcomes across NSW. Key Responsibilities Deliver engaging professional development workshops on early childhood road safety education. Build positive relationships with education and care services, tertiary providers, and community organisations. Facilitate learning for diverse audiences including educators, families, management teams, and pre-service teachers. Travel regularly throughout greater Sydney to support workshop delivery and stakeholder engagement.   About You You are a confident educator and presenter who enjoys working with adults as well as children. You are self-motivated, adaptable, and capable of working independently while maintaining strong professional relationships. Essential Requirements Four-year Early Childhood Education degree or equivalent ACECQA approved teaching qualification. Demonstrated success teaching in early childhood education and care settings. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Strong understanding of the diversity of early childhood education and care services. Experience working with children and families from diverse communities. Ability to work independently and respond effectively to unexpected situations. Ability to travel throughout the greater Sydney region and to undertake regular evening workshops and occasional weekend work. Current unrestricted NSW Driver Licence. Current Working with Children Check. A medical clearance, demerit point check and National Police Check will be carried out for successful applicants.   Desirable Experience facilitating adult learning or professional development. Experience or knowledge of road safety education.   Why Join Kids and Traffic ? Kids and Traffic is the leading provider of early childhood road safety education in NSW. The Program is in its fourth decade of a shared governance partnership between Transport for NSW, Macquarie University, the NSW Department of Education, Catholic Schools NSW, and Independent Schools NSW. Working within a respected statewide program, you'll have the opportunity to: Engage with educators and communities across NSW Work with a highly regarded team of education professionals Apply your teaching expertise in a unique and rewarding specialist role Make a positive impact on children's safety and wellbeing.   Apply Now To be considered for this position, you must submit a cover letter addressing the essential criteria and your CV. Applicants must be legally entitled to work in Australia.    Applicants are strongly encouraged to contact Louise Cosgrove – Acting Program Director, Kids and Traffic , on 0408283084 or louise.cosgrove@mq.edu.au for further information about the role. For any general recruitment enquiries please contact Mirna Alaadian mirna.alaaiddin@mq.edu.au If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 07/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Senior-Education-Developer_R000024722": {
      "title": "Senior Education Developer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n$126,306 – $140,543 per annum (HEW Level 8) and 17% superannuation and annual leave loading Full-time, fixed term for 12 months (two positions available) Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Macquarie University is reimagining the student learning experience. As part of the Macquarie Advantage, Education for Future Generations, a university-wide project is underway to integrate Microsoft Teams into the student learning environment, complementing iLearn to create a more dynamic, interactive and connected experience for students. With more than 2,450 units offered across all teaching periods in 2026, the scale of the opportunity and the impact is significant. To deliver this, we are recruiting two Senior Education Developers for a 12-month term within the Office of the Pro Vice-Chancellor (Education), working closely with Digital Transformation team, IT, Faculty and Macquarie Academy learning designers. You will be at the centre of discovery, design, development and delivery: building practical digital learning solutions, then equipping academic and professional staff to use them with confidence through training and effective handover. This is a hands-on role for someone who enjoys the idea of bringing Microsoft Teams to life in the digital classroom environment. If you are energised by technology-enhanced learning, evidence-informed design and the chance to influence practice across an entire university, we would like to hear from you. About the Role Reporting to the Head, Operations and Strategic Delivery (PVCE), you will design and deliver technology-enhanced learning solutions across a diverse range of courses and programs and provide expert advice that shapes how online and blended learning is delivered at Macquarie. Key responsibilities include: Designing and producing high-quality, technology-enhanced digital learning solutions that meet agreed timelines, quality standards and budget parameters. Providing expert consultancy, advice and training to academic staff, learning designers and central partners to shape online and blended learning strategies and create seamless student experiences across digital environments. Evaluating pedagogical effectiveness throughout development and at project completion, analysing feedback and impact data to inform evidence-based improvements. Embedding the University's vision and imperatives and meeting statutory and policy obligations, including accessibility, while designing for employability, reuse and syndication where appropriate. Establishing digital design standards and tools, including templates, project planning resources and functional specifications, and encouraging consistent adoption of agreed procedures and quality benchmarks across the academic community. Managing learning technology development projects end-to-end: scoping work, coordinating multidisciplinary contributions (such as video, audio, visual design and programming specialists), maintaining clear stakeholder communication and delivering sustainable, achievable outcomes. Keeping pace with university, national and international developments, including digital and AI-enabled pedagogies, and translating insights into practical improvements and strategic recommendations. About Us Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . About You (Selection Criteria) You are an experienced education or learning developer who combines pedagogical insight with practical digital expertise. You are comfortable advising academic colleagues, translating requirements into functional digital solutions, and managing multiple projects in a complex environment. You bring sound professional judgement, initiative, and a genuine interest in what makes learning work for students. A relevant tertiary qualification in technology, instructional design or a related field, and/or an equivalent combination of qualifications and extensive relevant experience. Substantial experience designing and developing digital education programs in a higher education context, including engaging online and blended learning experiences – ideally using Moodle/iLearn and Microsoft Teams. Demonstrated expertise navigating technologies, systems and digital environments to create streamlined experiences for students, academic and professional staff. Demonstrated ability to integrate AI meaningfully and effectively into education learning environments. High-level communication, consultation and relationship-building skills, with the ability to advise and train colleagues across a range of disciplines. Well-developed organisational and project coordination skills, including the ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines in a complex environment. Capacity to work with autonomy and initiative while contributing effectively as part of a multidisciplinary team, applying sound professional judgement. Experience contributing to institution-wide learning and teaching initiatives, and knowledge of the Australian higher education policy and regulatory environment and its implications for learning, teaching and assessment. (Desirable)   How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applications Close : Applications will close on Wednesday 21st October at 11.59 PM. Why Join Us? We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University: Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 21/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Research-Assistant--Animal-and-Cellular-Specialist-_R000024682": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Animal and Cellular Specialist)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTo provide research, technical and administrative support for research projects developing novel therapeutics to treat neurological disorders such as Alzheimer’s disease and epilepsy. · Salary package - From 88,670 per annum (HEW Level 4) plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading   · Appointment type – Full-time fixed term contract for 1 year   · Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde   Advance dementia and epilepsy research, apply your laboratory expertise and help move discoveries towards new therapies   Alzheimer's disease and epilepsy remain among the most complex challenges in neuroscience. At Macquarie University's Dementia Research Centre, researchers are working at the interface of molecular biology, animal models and cell-based systems to develop novel therapeutics for these disorders. We are seeking a Research Assistant to provide the research, technical and administrative expertise that keeps this work moving forward.  Reporting to A/Prof Janet van Eersel, you will be hands-on across the full research pipeline - from maintaining and characterising the mouse colony and conducting behavioural, motor and memory testing, through to molecular and biochemical analysis of tissue and cultured cells. You will contribute to experimental planning, data analysis and the preparation of research outputs, while helping to keep the laboratory running smoothly and safely day to day.  This is an opportunity to build deep technical capability within a well-resourced, interdisciplinary centre that sits inside Australia's first fully integrated academic health sciences centre. If you enjoy varied laboratory work, precise technique and research with a clear translational purpose, this role will give you both breadth and depth.  About the Role   As a Research Assistant, you will:  Monitor and maintain the mouse colony to a high standard, assisting with breeding, weaning offspring, health monitoring, monitoring pregnancies, genotyping and record keeping  Carry out and assist with behavioural, motor and memory testing of mice, including analysis of digital behavioural data  Assist with animal surgeries, treatment administration and tissue harvesting  Conduct biochemical analysis of biological samples (cell culture and animal tissue) using techniques such as Western blotting, immunohistochemistry, PCR and protein extraction  Undertake molecular biology experiments including RT-PCR, DNA/RNA extraction, molecular cloning and modification of DNA plasmids  Culture, treat and analyse cell lines, induced pluripotent stem cells, embryonic stem cells and primary cells, using methods such as immunocytochemical staining and Western blot  Contribute to the planning and conduct of experiments in line with scientific standards, and assist HDR students and other staff with straightforward research techniques  Maintain accurate records and data management, monitor consumable stock levels, and help keep the laboratory compliant with work health and safety requirements, SOPs and SWPs  Assist with data analysis, statistical evaluation, and the preparation of research data, reports and scientific manuscripts for publication  About Us   Macquarie University has the nation's first fully integrated academic health sciences centre under a university's leadership. With a focus on patients and an ultimate goal of improving lives, the Macquarie University Health Sciences Centre (MQ Health) is a true convergence of the learning and research endeavours of Macquarie's Faculty of Medicine, Health and Human Sciences with the clinical care provided at Macquarie University Hospital and Clinics. It brings together the work of medical and allied health researchers across the University and around the country, with unparalleled access to the world-leading clinical resources and research facilities found only on our campus.  The Dementia Research Centre, part of the Macquarie Medical School, provides an environment for innovative, interdisciplinary dementia research, using and developing state-of-the-art technologies to advance basic discoveries towards translation into clinical treatments. The Centre offers a team-based research environment for cutting-edge science, with a shared vision of developing novel therapeutics to treat these devastating disorders.  About You   You are a laboratory-based scientist with hands-on experience across animal and cell-based research techniques, and you take pride in precise technique, accurate records and reliable results. You are organised, methodical and comfortable managing multiple experiments in a busy research setting, and you communicate clearly with colleagues and students.  Selection Criteria   Bachelor's degree with Honours or Masters in medical science, neuroscience, biochemistry or a related discipline (a PhD in a related discipline will be highly regarded)  Experience in animal care, handling and behavioural analysis  Experience with laboratory techniques such as PCR, DNA and protein extraction, Western blotting, immunohistochemistry, molecular biology and cell culture  Experience working in a research laboratory, with a thorough understanding of laboratory health and safety practices and principles  Knowledge of laboratory administration and experimental planning  Well-developed organisational and time management skills, with a demonstrated capacity to meet tight deadlines  Clear written and verbal communication skills, including the preparation and presentation of research data, and experience working both autonomously and as part of a research team    How to Apply   To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above).  Applications Close: Wednesday 21st October, 11:59pm AEST    We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date.   **This position is not available for visa sponsorship, and the successful applicant must have valid work rights in Australia for the full 1-year fixed-term contract**     For General enquiries: Rebecca Wood, Talent Acquisition at r.wood@mq.edu.au     Why Join Us?   Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today .  We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University.  Flexible, hybrid work arrangements  17% Superannuation  Subsidised onsite parking options  Extensive training and professional development programs  Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents  Onsite vacation care during school holidays  Discounted health insurance  Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre  Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support  Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 21/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Program-Officer--Girls-to-Graduates_R000024553": {
      "title": "Program Officer, Girls to Graduates",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\n· Salary Package: From $102,136 per annum (HEW 6), plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading (pro-rata rates apply for part-time positions) · Appointment Type: Part-time (28 hours per week), fixed term until 30 June 2031 · Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Create pathways into STEMM education and careers, build meaningful partnerships with students, schools and communities, and help transform opportunities for girls and women. At Macquarie University, we are committed to creating a more diverse and inclusive STEMM (Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine) workforce. Despite progress, girls and women continue to be underrepresented across STEMM study and career pathways, with those from equity backgrounds often facing additional barriers to participation and success. The Girls to Graduates (G2G) program is a flagship equity initiative that addresses these challenges by creating pathways, building confidence and capability and supporting girls and women from diverse backgrounds to pursue and succeed in STEMM. Delivered through a whole-of-university approach, G2G brings together faculties, professional staff, students, schools and industry partners to strengthen participation and progression across the STEMM pipeline. Funded through the Australian Government's Women in STEM and Entrepreneurship (WISE) Round 5 program, G2G is a dedicated five-year initiative designed to create sustainable and lasting impact. As the Program Officer, you will join a collaborative project team responsible for designing and delivering outreach, access and participation initiatives on campus and in partnership with schools, industry partners and stakeholders across the University. One day you might be facilitating a campus experience day for secondary students; the next, co-designing a new activity with an industry partner, briefing a group of student ambassadors, or reviewing evaluation data to improve program outcomes. It is varied, practical, people-focused work that contributes directly to increasing the participation, success and leadership of girls and women in STEMM. Working within the Office of the Pro Vice-Chancellor (Education), you will be part of a small, purpose-driven team delivering a significant university-wide initiative in collaboration with faculties, operational units and external partners. If you enjoy building relationships, coordinating impactful programs and turning good ideas into meaningful outcomes, this is an opportunity to contribute to a long-term effort to transform opportunities for girls and women in STEMM and see the impact of your work reflected in the aspirations and achievements of the students you support. About the Role Reporting to the Girls to Graduates Program Coordinator, you will contribute to the planning, delivery, evaluation and continuous improvement of the Girls to Graduates program. Key responsibilities include: In consultation with the relevant Coordinator, designing and delivering STEMM-focused outreach, access and participation initiatives, both on campus and in collaboration with school and industry partners. Developing and sustaining productive relationships with schools, industry partners and internal Macquarie stakeholders to enable program delivery. Contributing to the research, development and best-practice implementation of evidence-informed STEMM equity programs and initiatives that support participation, retention and success. Assisting with the evaluation and continuous improvement of programs and initiatives, including monitoring and reporting on reach and impact. Recruiting, training, rostering and supervising casual and volunteer staff, including student ambassadors, who participate in program delivery. Working as part of the wider Access and Widening Participation team and contributing to the University’s strategic objective for equity of participation, and performing other duties as required and permitted by this classification under the MQ Professional Staff Enterprise Agreement Complying with relevant EEO and WHS regulations About Us Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation in 1964, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we've grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . The Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Academic) portfolio has overall accountability for the planning, quality and delivery of education at Macquarie. Within it, the Pro Vice-Chancellor (Education) oversees the full educational lifecycle, including pathways and access, curriculum and educational capability, graduate success and Macquarie University College. The Access and Widening Participation unit advances the University's equity agenda by improving access to, participation in, and success within higher education for students from backgrounds that have been historically underrepresented — including First Nations students, students from low socio-economic status backgrounds, and those from regional and remote communities. About You You are an organised, practical program professional who enjoys working with young people, schools and community partners. You bring sound project coordination skills, clear communication, and knowledge of the systemic and structural factors that affect girls’ and women’s participation, retention and advancement in STEMM studies and careers. You are comfortable juggling multiple competing activities, adapting plans when circumstances change, and using evidence to make programs better. Selection Criteria A tertiary qualification and/or extensive relevant experience in a related area, Demonstrated knowledge of systemic, cultural and structural factors influencing girl’s and women’s participation, retention and advancement in STEMM studies, careers and leadership, Proven project management skills, including evaluation and continuous improvement of programs, Excellent written and oral communication skills, including the ability to communicate thoughtfully and respectfully with diverse audiences, Well-developed relationship-building skills, including experience working with key stakeholders in partner schools and communities, High-level skills in the use of Office 365, including the ability to prepare engaging materials for school and tertiary students, and Experience recruiting and managing casual staff and/or volunteers, and the ability to work proactively as part of a cross-functional team. *** The successful applicant will be required to undergo a police check and must hold a current NSW Working with Children Check, or be willing to obtain one. They must also hold a current NSW driver’s licence and be available for occasional out-of-hours work and regional travel. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience meets the selection criteria (above). Applications Close: Thursday 29 October 2026 at 11:59 p.m. *** We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. We also reserve the right to close the advertisement early if a sufficient number of qualified applicants is received. For enquiries about the role, please contact Jacinta Carruthers, Head, Access and Widening Participation at jacinta.carruthers@mq.edu.au , or Melissa Wong at melissa.wong@mq.edu.au . Why Join Us? We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Our prime location is just a short walk from Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Shopping Centre. Enjoy the benefits of working at a campus that offers: 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Flexible working options Training and professional development Onsite childcare facilities Discounted health insurance (Medibank) Onsite vacation care Employee Assistance Program Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 29/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Faculty-Administration-Officer_R000024733": {
      "title": "Faculty Administration Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n· Salary Package: From $102,136 per annum (HEW 6), plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading · Appointment Type: Full-time, continuing · Faculty of Arts, Macquarie University (Wallumattagal Campus), North Ryde Keep Faculty operations moving, enable senior staff and help shape one of Australia's foremost arts and humanities communities. The Faculty of Arts at Macquarie University is home to bold thinkers and dedicated educators asking the big questions about the world, from history, languages and media to law, security studies, education and the creative arts. As the Faculty Administration Officer, you will provide administrative support to the Faculty Executive Director and support with Faculty strategic priorities. This is an excellent opportunity for an organised, proactive administrator who enjoys variety, thrives on getting things done well, and takes genuine pride in high-quality service. If you like being the person who anticipates what is needed next, brings order to competing priorities and makes operational delivery look effortless, we would like to hear from you. About the Role   Reporting to the Faculty Executive Director, you will:  Provide general administrative support to the Faculty leadership team including supporting Faculty strategic priorities. Deliver executive assistance to the Faculty Executive Director , including diary management, logistics, meeting preparation, travel arrangements and briefing materials.  Coordinate Faculty committees, including scheduling, agenda preparation, minute-taking and follow-up of action items.  Organise on-site and off-site meetings, including room bookings, catering, transport and event logistics.  Update and maintain Faculty websites and administrative systems.  Receive, triage and action enquiries relating to the Faculty's activities.  Provide coordination and administration for Faculty events.  Assist with administrative services as required.  Contribute to the review and improvement of administrative processes and practices.  Work in accordance with EEO, WHS and relevant professional standards.  About Us   Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation in 1964, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we've grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today .  Within the University, the Faculty of Arts is one of Australia’s leading arts and humanities faculties, bringing together a diverse community of educators, researchers and professional staff. Its professional staff work in partnership with academic colleagues to support the faculty’s teaching, research and engagement through high-quality administrative services.   About You   You are a capable, service-oriented administrator with experience supporting senior leadership positions. You manage multiple priorities with ease, work comfortably with minimal supervision as well as alongside colleagues, and communicate clearly with people at all levels. You are ready to step in wherever needed, bring a can-do approach, a willingness to learn and support a positive culture, while remaining composed when the pace picks up. Your attention to detail, continuous improvement approach and ability to build positive working relationships across a wide range of stakeholders will be central to your success.  Selection Criteria   A degree in Business Administration and/or equivalent relevant experience.  Demonstrated experience delivering high-quality administrative and/or executive assistance within a complex organisational environment (higher education experience desirable), including assisting senior staff and their teams.  Proven ability to coordinate multiple activities and priorities with minimal supervision and to meet tight deadlines.  Demonstrated high-quality customer service experience, with the ability to communicate effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders.  Intermediate computer skills, including Microsoft Office and a range of database management systems and applications.  Excellent attention to detail, with demonstrated experience developing and implementing administrative process improvements.  Exceptional written communication skills with the ability to draft agendas, minutes and reports for a senior executive audience.  Demonstrated knowledge of finance and budgeting principles and practices, including budget administration, interpreting data and using financial systems and reporting.  *** The successful candidate will be required to undertake a police check.   How to Apply   To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience meets the selection criteria (above).  Please note: Applicants must have full unrestricted working rights in Australia.  Applications Close: Sunday 1 November 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEDT)   *** We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date.   For role enquiries or recruitment enquiries, please contact Joanne Chrystal, Faculty Executive Director at FOAExecutiveDirector@mq.edu.au , or Mirna Alaaiddin at mirna.alaaiddin@mq.edu.au Why Join Us?   We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability.  Our prime location is just a short walk from Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Shopping Centre. Enjoy the benefits of working at a campus that offers:  17% Superannuation  Subsidised onsite parking options  Flexible working options  Training and professional development  Onsite childcare facilities  Discounted health insurance (Medibank)  Onsite vacation care  Employee Assistance Program  Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre  Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics  Pre-Employment Checks   Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 01/11/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Housekeeper_R000024748": {
      "title": "Housekeeper",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nJoin Lakeside Hotel as a housekeeper for day shifts. Clean rooms, restock amenities, and help guests. Requires cleaning experience and AU work rights. As a Housekeeper, you will work within the housekeeping team performing a variety of tasks to ensure guest room is correctly set up, cared for, and maintained to ensure the hotel and public areas are serviced and presented to the highest standards for all guests. You will liaise with guests to assist with any queries as required, while maintaining guest safety and privacy.   Duties include Cleaning guestrooms and restocking guestroom amenities Making beds & replacing dirty linens and towels Removing garbage, recycling, and room service trays Available shifts for this role are between 8 am and 4 pm, Monday to Sunday. ABOUT YOU With some previous experience working in a hotel housekeeping department or commercial cleaning setting, you have strong attention to detail and take pride in your work. You have good organisational skills and understanding of workplace health & safety. You will be able to work independently and be a proactive team member. ABOUT US Lakeside Hotel and Conference Centre, operate an award-winning venue situated on the picturesque grounds of Macquarie University Lake. The conference centre is a seven-days’ a week operation, providing a suite of services that support the operation of U@MQ, the wider Macquarie University Community and Non-University business, and include 4 star 40-room hotel, restaurant, bar, café and multipurpose function rooms.  To Apply Upload your CV and a short cover letter outlining your suitability for the role as part of the online application process.  Applicants must be legally entitled to work in Australia. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 14/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Member-Experience-Officer_R000024201": {
      "title": "Member Experience Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nAn exciting and fast-paced customer service role based in a busy gym that contributes to a great experience for our members. Our Member Experience team is a key function within our centre. As one of our Member Experience Officers you will be: Providing a consistent and high level of service to members and guests to drive acquisition and member retention. Responding to and actioning customer queries in-person, over the phone and via email. Executing acquisition and retention strategies and campaigns to sell memberships. Following established processes and procedures for memberships, point of sale transactions, cash handling, end-to-end venue hire bookings, and administration processes associated with the Centres operations and safety policy. Respond to member and guest feedback, providing constructive information to continuously improve outcomes that support a positive customer experience. About You To be successful in this role you will need: Proven experience in a front-line customer facing role. Demonstrated success in achieving sales targets, prioritising tasks, and meeting deadlines. A proven record of accomplishment in the area of customer experience and continuous improvement. Well-developed interpersonal and communication skills including the ability to work collaboratively and to establish, build and maintain respectful and ethical relationships with staff, students, and other key stakeholders. Excellent organisational and time management skills and attention to detail. Proficient skills in Microsoft Office applications, including database management. This role requires a criminal history check, First Aid and CPR certificate. Standard work hours will require you to be available on weekends, early mornings and evenings to meet the needs of the business. About Us Macquarie University Sport and Aquatic Centre (MUSAC) is a multi-purpose venue designed to help meet all the health, fitness and sporting needs of our members and guests. Our facilities include a 6-lane heated indoor pool, and an 8-lane outdoor heated Olympic-sized swimming pool. The centre features a fully equipped health club, group and virtual fitness classes, squash courts, gymnastics / aquatics programs and social sports. Macquarie University Sport Fields operates 7 days a week, our facilities include 5 professional playing fields which accommodates a variety of events, stadium lighting, canteen and BBQ areas, and four change rooms. Benefits: Complementary Macquarie University Sport & Aquatic Centre gym access Access to our staff wellbeing program and staff support services  Working on a vibrant parkland campus, with a huge variety of food & beverage outlets, and general practice & hospital amenities Access to discounted corporate health insurance and employee flu shot program Staff discounts at Campus Life operated hospitality outlets To Apply: If being part of an inclusive, vibrant, team orientated organisation is something you are passionate about we encourage you to apply.   In the first instance, general enquiries should be directed to Xavier Maniacara on 02 9850 1022, or via email xavier.maniacara@mq.edu.au . To be considered for this position, you must submit your CV and a cover letter addressing the listed criteria in the About You section via our online application portal. If you need any support or reasonable adjustments through this recruitment process, please let us know so we can provide the support you need. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 19/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Knowledge-Specialist_R000024742": {
      "title": "Knowledge Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\n- Casual opportunity - Service Improvement Program - $74.36 per hour (HEW 8) + 25% casual loading + 12% super - Enjoy a vibrant on-campus location, close to public transport Shape how research knowledge is captured, curated and reused – and see your work applied at scale In this role, you will design the knowledge environment for Macquarie University's Research Program – the frameworks, taxonomies, repositories, and content that make evidence, methodologies and lessons learned genuinely accessible to researchers, professional staff, industry and community partners. Reporting to the Research Program Manager within Service Improvement, you will work across a program that brings diverse expertise into one place. If you enjoy moving between design and practical delivery – this role offers real scope to make a difference. About the Role As Knowledge Specialist – Research Program, you will: Develop and implement the Research Program Knowledge Management Plan Build and maintain SharePoint knowledge repositories, knowledge bases, FAQs, templates and guidance materials Draft, edit, curate and publish knowledge articles, research insights, lessons learned, methodologies and research resources Gather content from researchers and subject matter experts, translating complex information into accessible, plain-language content Maintain knowledge article trackers and publication schedules, and monitor milestones, risks, issues and deliverables against knowledge management plans Conduct content reviews and audits so that knowledge assets remain current, accurate and useful Test and refine search functionality (AI), keywords, and user experience Facilitate workshops and stakeholder engagement meetings, as required Provide training to lift knowledge management capability across the program Advance continuous improvement and wider adoption of knowledge management practice About Us Service Improvement partners across the University to deliver programs that change how our people work. The Research Program brings together researchers and professional staff to generate, translate and apply knowledge – and this role makes certain that knowledge endures well beyond any single project. About You You are an experienced knowledge or information management practitioner who is as comfortable analysing content and building knowledge capability. You translate complexity into clarity, you know your way around SharePoint, and you build credibility quickly with researchers and senior stakeholders in busy, evolving environments. Selection Criteria Tertiary qualifications in Information Management, Research Management, or a related discipline, with equivalent experience also considered Demonstrated hands-on capability with SharePoint, knowledge bases, and content management systems, including search optimisation and user experience testing Proven track record creating, editing, and publishing knowledge articles, guidance materials and templates for varied audiences Experience working with subject matter experts and stakeholders in complex or matrixed environments Well-developed reporting, project coordination, and stakeholder engagement capability, including preparation of papers for governance forums Capacity to combine plan with day-to-day operational delivery, alongside experience facilitating workshops, training, or communities of practice How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applications Close: 11:59pm AEDT, 30 October 2026 We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact Swati Srivastava, Head of Commercial at swati.srivastava@mq.edu.au Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you are already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you will need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 30/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/English-for-Academic-Purposes-Teachers_R000024774-1": {
      "title": "English for Academic Purposes Teachers",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-14\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nExpressions of interest are invited for casual teaching opportunities in English for Academic Purposes programs at Macquarie University College. The Role Macquarie University College  within Macquarie University, is currently inviting expressions of interest from appropriately qualified and experienced teachers for our English Language Intensive Courses for Overseas Students (ELICOS) programs. As a teacher with us, you are expected to: ·       be up to date with contemporary teaching methodology to prepare and deliver EAP lessons, ·       mark assessments and provide targeted, meaningful feedback ·       undertake student consultation, ·       work collaboratively with staff and students, ·       supervise in-class assessments and examinations, ·       manage and submit results, and ·       closely monitor and report on student progress and attendance About Us Macquarie University College provides local and international students with an alternative pathway to the University’s undergraduate degree offerings, and the English Language Program prepares international students for university study through the delivery of English language and academic literacy programs. About You You are a dedicated teaching professional with qualifications and experience in English language teaching. You have the expertise and enthusiasm to motivate and educate students in a high-stakes EAP program. Selection Criteria Qualified English Language teacher with a minimum of: ·       A recognised 3-year degree or equivalent; and ·       A recognised pre-service TESOL certificate with practicum component of no less than 6 hours supervised practice; and ·       Up to and including 3 years full-time English for Academic Purposes teaching experience ·       The ability to operate and adapt in a fast-paced environment ·       Preparedness to work collaboratively with staff and students ·       Good administrative skills and attention to detail   Desired Criteria ·       Master of Applied Linguistics/TESOL/Education or equivalent ·       IELTS or Cambridge examiner experience Successful Expressions of Interest will be kept on file and may be considered by the College when a vacancy arises that is an appropriate match to their skill base, disciplinary background and availability. *** Neither having an Expression of Interest on file nor being considered for a vacancy imply that employment is guaranteed. Please note that by providing an Expression of Interest for these positions, you agree that your details may be placed on file for a period of 24 months.  To Apply To be considered for this position, please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter no more than 2 pages that outlines how you meet the selection criteria. Enquiries: For role related enquiries, please contact Cara Dinneen at  cara.dinneen@mq.edu.au Application Closing Date : Sunday 25 October 2026 at 11:59 PM (AEDT).    If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 24/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Finance-Business-Partner_R000024808-1": {
      "title": "Finance Business Partner",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-13\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTo provide a high level of executive support and management of financial performance to Macquarie University Health. Competitive annual package circa $172K (including superannuation) Full-time, continuing contract Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde   Financial expertise meets strategic impact in Australia’s only integrated academic Health precinct. About the role   We are seeking an experienced Finance Business Partner to join our Macquarie University Health finance team, where you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the financial performance and future success of Macquarie University Hospital and Health Clinics (MQ Health).   As a Finance Business Partner, you will work as a trusted advisor, partnering closely with senior stakeholders to provide critical financial insights and drive business decision-making. This is an opportunity to combine your financial expertise with your leadership and strategic capabilities to make a meaningful impact across a unique healthcare operation.   The Finance Business Partner works at the intersection of finance and strategy, translating complex data into actionable intelligence that drives business outcomes. This is a high impact role where you will partner directly with the Hospital Leadership and senior Health Finance and Commercial Managers in supporting desired strategic outcomes.   What will you do   Partner strategically with key stakeholders to understand their business needs and provide expert financial guidance that influences direction and decision-making. Drive business performance through insightful analysis, scenario modelling, and cost-benefit evaluations that support new initiatives and strategic imperatives. Lead continuous improvement activities within business units, that embed efficient finance processes. Shape financial planning by partnering with business units to develop and critically evaluate annual budgets, forecasts, and long-term financial plans. Deliver high-impact analysis and insights through month-end analyses and management information that tell the story behind the numbers.   About You: (Selection Criteria)   You have experience as a Finance Business Partner managing multiple stakeholders ideally within a large and complex healthcare (or similar) environment. With business partnering expertise, sound knowledge of commercial finance and the external finance landscape, you can apply this knowledge to support and influence stakeholders across all levels to ensure delivery. In addition, you will have the following:   Professional credentials – CA/CPA or equivalent qualification. Substantial experience – At least 4 years post CA/CPA experience in similar roles within large, complex organisations. Business partnering excellence – Proven ability to build rapport and influence senior stakeholders with trust and credibility. Financial Modelling – including scenario analysis and presenting actionable insights to support strategy and decision making. Commercial acumen – Sharp business insight combined with experience applying strong accounting principles. Advanced technical skills – Expertise in financial modelling, scenario analysis, and Microsoft Office (particularly Excel and PowerPoint).   Experience as a Finance Business Partner in the hospital, healthcare or similar sector is highly advantageous.   Why work at Macquarie     Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Celebrating its 60th year in 2024, it was established as a bold experiment in higher education and designed to break from educational traditions to work in tandem with industry. Institutionally we strive for the extraordinary by challenging convention and embracing different views. Our pioneering culture has encouraged and inspired students, staff and collaborators to break free from conventional thinking, and to actively shape the complex issues that define the future of humanity Connect with us today .    MQ Health Finance is a stand-alone finance function for Macquarie University Health.  It provides dedicated end-to-end Financial Performance and Business Partnering and support within the matrix structure of the broader Group Finance organization.  This stand-alone approach reflects the importance of MQ Health to the University Group, as its largest controlled entity with turnover in excess of $200M – approx. 20% of total Group revenues.  MQ Health has also recently made a step change in profitability, lifting from a historical break-even baseline to a sustained outlook for $15M+ in Operating Cash (EBITDA) each year.   Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity.  Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.   Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.   How to apply   Please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter that outlines how your experience is aligned to the role against the selection criteria.   *Please note this position requires criminal record check.   Applications Close:   Sunday 25 October at 11:59pm AEDT   We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 25/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Financial-Planning-and-Analysis-Analyst_R000024784-1": {
      "title": "Financial Planning and Analysis Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-13\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTo support financial planning, management reporting and analysis across Macquarie University Health including providing support to senior members in the Finance Planning and Analysis team. Base salary from $114,992 - $124,676 (HEW Level 7), plus 17% superannuation Full-time continuing role Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde   About the role We’re looking for a commercially minded and analytically driven Financial Planning & Analysis (FP&A) Analyst to join our high performing finance team at Macquarie University Health . This role offers the opportunity to work across a diverse healthcare enterprise, providing financial insights, forecasting and performance analysis that support operational and strategic decision making. Working closely with Finance colleagues and operational stakeholders, you will contribute to financial planning, performance reporting and business analysis while supporting improvements in financial systems, processes and reporting capabilities for Macquarie University Health. What you will do Analyse financial and operational performance, including revenue, expenditure, workforce and activity trends, to identify key drivers, risks and opportunities. Prepare monthly and quarterly management reports, providing meaningful analysis and commentary on financial performance. Develop budget templates, forecasts and long-term financial plans for Macquarie University Health, including capital projections, assumption validation and system uploads. Support the preparation of detailed 5-year budgets (including capital) for senior Finance stakeholders. Build financial models, evaluations and cost-benefit analyses to support business cases, service planning and operational improvements. Support the enhancement of reporting, planning and business intelligence systems, collaborating with IT to improve data quality, automation and workflows Build and maintain stakeholder relationships across Finance and the broader business, addressing financial enquiries and coordinating with operational managers About Us Macquarie University Health is Macquarie University's integrated health and medical enterprise, encompassing Macquarie University Hospital, medical imaging, mental health services (Mindspot) and a network of more than 20 specialist clinics. As the University's largest controlled entity, it generates annual turnover in excess of $200 million. Given the scale, complexity and commercial nature of Macquarie University Health's operations, it is supported by a dedicated Finance function that provides end-to-end financial performance management and business partnering. Operating within the broader Macquarie University Group Finance structure, Macquarie University Health Finance serves as a critical enabler of informed decision-making across a uniquely diverse and fast-growing health enterprise. About you (Selection Criteria) You have expertise in conducting research and analysis with a commercial focus, within a large organisation with complex accounting and reporting requirements. Experience in FP&A in a healthcare context would be an advantage. You are an excellent communicator, and thrive in fast-paced, dynamic environments. You build and maintain good, respectful relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders, consistently demonstrating professionalism and a collaborative mindset to achieve shared outcomes. Tertiary qualification in Accounting, Finance or a related discipline. Relevant experience in accounting, finance, or equivalent. Proven ability to build and apply financial models and conduct scenario analyses. Strong experience in forecasting financials, budget preparation and financial modelling to produce business models. Strong analytical skills with the ability to manipulate and interpret large volumes of financial and operational data, identify material issues and communicate findings clearly. Business Intelligence systems and reporting platforms skills e.g. PowerBI, Tableau, Cognos TM1, Calumo. Advanced Microsoft Office skills (particularly Excel and PowerPoint). Strong experience working with large Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) systems (preferably FinanceOne). *Please note this role requires a criminal record check. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applications Close: 25 October 2026 We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 25/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Finance-Business-Partner_R000024791-1": {
      "title": "Finance Business Partner",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-13\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCompetitive annual package circa $195K (including superannuation) Full-time, continuing contract Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde   Where financial expertise meets strategic impact. About the role   Are you a seasoned finance professional with a passion for driving business success through strategic advice and meaningful financial insights? We're seeking an experienced Finance Business Partner to join our Group Finance team at Macquarie University, where you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the financial performance and future success of our organisation.   At Macquarie University, we are committed to engaging and empowering the brightest minds to achieve extraordinary outcomes. As a Finance Business Partner, you will work as a trusted advisor, partnering closely with senior stakeholders to provide critical financial insights and drive business decision-making. This is an opportunity to combine your financial expertise with your leadership and strategic capabilities to make a meaningful impact across a diverse and innovative organisation.   The Finance Business Partner works at the intersection of finance and strategy, translating complex data into actionable intelligence that drives business outcomes. This is a high impact role where you will work within the Vice-President Finance and Resources portfolio substantively supporting the property team managing complex physical asset expenditure and budgeting. This position also supports the portfolio of the Vice-President Strategy, Planning and Performance.   What will you do   Partner strategically with key stakeholders to understand their business needs and provide expert financial guidance that influences direction and decision-making. Drive business performance through insightful analysis, scenario modelling, and cost-benefit evaluations that support new initiatives and strategic imperatives. Lead continuous improvement activities within business units, that embed efficient finance processes. Shape financial planning by partnering with business units to develop and critically evaluate annual budgets, forecasts, and long-term financial plans. Deliver high-impact analysis and insights through month-end analyses and management information that tell the story behind the numbers.   About You: (Selection Criteria)   You have experience as a Finance Business Partner managing multiple stakeholders within a large organisation with complex accounting and reporting needs. With sound knowledge of commercial finance and the external finance landscape, you can apply this knowledge to support and influence stakeholders across all levels to ensure delivery. In addition, you will have the following:   Professional credentials – CA/CPA or equivalent qualification. Substantial experience –  At least 4 years post CA/CPA experience in similar roles within large, complex organisations. Business partnering excellence – Proven ability to build rapport and influence senior stakeholders with trust and credibility. Financial Modelling – including scenario analysis and presenting actionable insights to support strategy and decision making. Commercial acumen – Sharp business insight combined with experience applying strong accounting principles. Advanced technical skills – Expertise in financial modelling, scenario analysis, and Microsoft Office (particularly Excel and PowerPoint).   Experience as a Finance Business Partner in the property, construction, or asset management sectors would be highly advantageous.   Why work at Macquarie     Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Celebrating its 60th year in 2024, it was established as a bold experiment in higher education and designed to break from educational traditions to work in tandem with industry. Institutionally we strive for the extraordinary by challenging convention and embracing different views. Our pioneering culture has encouraged and inspired students, staff and collaborators to break free from conventional thinking, and to actively shape the complex issues that define the future of humanity Connect with us today .    We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the staff benefits on offer.   Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity.  Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.   Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.   How to apply   Please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter that outlines how your experience is aligned to the role against the selection criteria.   *Please note this position requires criminal record check.   For a confidential conversation please contact Sarah Bate, Head of Talent Acquisition via sarah.bate@mq.edu.au .   Applications Close:   Tuesday 27 October at 11:59pm AEDT   We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 27/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
